   <caption unique="1261276">Instruction Operand Encoding</caption>
   </table>
  </operand_table>
 <longdesc><para unique="1261278">Performs a bitwise XNOR between the vector mask k2 and the vector mask k3, and writes the result into vector mask k1 (three-operand form).</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1261280">KXNORW</title>
   <programlisting>DEST[15:0] := NOT (SRC1[15:0] BITWISE XOR SRC2[15:0])
DEST[MAX_KL-1:16] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1261284">KXNORB</title>
   <programlisting>DEST[7:0] := NOT (SRC1[7:0] BITWISE XOR SRC2[7:0])
DEST[MAX_KL-1:8] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1261288">KXNORQ</title>
   <programlisting>DEST[63:0] := NOT (SRC1[63:0] BITWISE XOR SRC2[63:0])
DEST[MAX_KL-1:64] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1261292">KXNORD</title>
   <programlisting>DEST[31:0] := NOT (SRC1[31:0] BITWISE XOR SRC2[31:0])
DEST[MAX_KL-1:32] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>KXNORW __mmask16 _mm512_kxnor(__mmask16 a, __mmask16 b);</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1261298">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1261300">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1261305" format="xIndent1">See <link unique="1261303" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#42536: 06_Table: Table 2-63. TYPE K20 Exception Definition (VEX-Encoded OpMask" xrefstyle="Table All - no page-period">Table&#160;2&#8209;65, &#8220;TYPE K20 Exception Definition (VEX-Encoded OpMask Instructions w/o Memory Arg).&#8221;</link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
